From c3f18d4ada45a825efb784934d9cd5f8e10f769a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:34:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: the log written off the game thread, a lock-free STR
 reader, stream/log/thread lines, LiveArea art

The profile's runs of slow frames (t04, t09, t10: 0.45-1.3 s each) were its own log: every
line was written and synced in place, about 0.42 s a line while the card was slow, and the
stall lines, written from the frame wait, made the next frame a stall too. stderr now goes
through a ring to a writer thread on cores 1-2, below the game thread's priority
(THPS_LOG_SYNC=1 keeps the old way); [log] gives the writes and the slowest sync every 10 s.

The STR reader: the game thread only reads and writes atomics (no semaphore signal each frame);
the reader looks every 4 ms, reads 16 sectors per sceIoRead, starts a song over with a seek,
and runs above the game thread's priority on core 2. [stream] comes every 10 s by the clock,
whatever the stream is doing, and [threads] gives each thread's core, priority, run time and
preemptions. Stall-line addresses (and PC_VitaLogOpen's) are printed without the Thumb bit.

LiveArea: icon0, bg and startup made from the two cover pictures (8-bit indexed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
